    "eligibility_criteria": "\ud83c\uddf2\ud83c\udde6 Eligibility Criteria for Moroccan Candidates (Crit\u00e8res d'\u00c9ligibilit\u00e9 pour les Candidats Marocains):\n\n1. Nationality: Holder of Moroccan Citizenship (Nationalit\u00e9 marocaine en cours de validit\u00e9).\n2. Educational Qualifications:\n   \u2022 For Master / Dipl\u00f4me d'Ing\u00e9nieur: Moroccan Baccalaureate (Baccalaur\u00e9at marocain toutes fili\u00e8res: Sciences Maths, PC, SVT, \u00c9co) or Moroccan Licence (Bac+3) / Master (Bac+5) / Dipl\u00f4me d'Ing\u00e9nieur d'\u00c9tat de l'ENCG, ENSA, FST, Facult\u00e9 des Sciences, etc.\n   \u2022 Academic Performance: Minimum GPA of 3.0/4.0 or Mention Assez Bien / Bien (Moyenne g\u00e9n\u00e9rale de 12/20 \u00e0 16/20+).\n3. Age Limits:\n   \u2022 Bachelor: Under 25 years old\n   \u2022 Master: Under 35 years old\n   \u2022 PhD: Under 40 years old\n4. Language Requirements:\n   \u2022 English-Taught Track: IELTS 6.0+, TOEFL iBT 80+, Duolingo 105+, OR Official English Proficiency Certificate from Moroccan faculty (Attestation de langue anglaise d\u00e9livr\u00e9e par l'\u00e9tablissement d'origine).\n   \u2022 Chinese-Taught Track: HSK Level 4 (180+ score) for Bachelor, HSK Level 5 (180+ score) for Master/PhD. (Note: Students without HSK can benefit from 1-Year Full Scholarship Chinese Language Foundation Year before starting degree!).",
    "required_education_level": "High School / Bachelor",
    "minimum_gpa": 3.0,
    "required_fields_of_study": "All Disciplines",
    "application_fee": "0.00",
    "required_documents": [
      "Valid Passport (Bio-data page, minimum 12 months validity)",
      "Notarized Highest Diploma (Moroccan Baccalaureate / Licence / Master with sworn Chinese or English translation)",
      "Official Academic Transcripts (Relev\u00e9s de notes de tous les semestres avec traduction asserment\u00e9e)",
      "Study Plan & Research Proposal (800+ words for Bachelor/Master, 1500+ words for PhD in English or Chinese)",
      "Two Academic Recommendation Letters (Lettres de recommandation sign\u00e9es par des professeurs universitaires marocains)",
      "Foreigner Physical Examination Form (Mod\u00e8le officiel d'examen m\u00e9dical avec ECG, radiographie pulmonaire et s\u00e9rologie)",
      "Non-Criminal Record Certificate / Casier Judiciaire (Extrait de casier judiciaire ou fiche anthropom\u00e9trique l\u00e9galis\u00e9e)",
      "Proof of Language Proficiency (IELTS 6.0+ / TOEFL 80+ / Duolingo / ou Attestation de langue anglaise d\u00e9livr\u00e9e par la facult\u00e9 marocaine)",
      "Pre-Acceptance Letter from Academic Advisor (Lettre de pr\u00e9-acceptation d'un professeur - Fortement recommand\u00e9e pour Master/Doctorat)",
      "Digital ID Passport Photos (Format 33x48mm fond blanc haute r\u00e9solution)"
    ],
    "application_instructions": "\ud83d\udccb Official Step-by-Step Application Guide for Moroccan Students (Proc\u00e9dure de Candidature Officielle):\n\nStep 1: CSC Chinese Government Scholarship Portal Registration:\n\u2022 Go to the official CSC portal: https://studyinchina.csc.edu.cn/ (or campuschina.org).\n\u2022 Create an account and select Program Category Type B (University Program applied directly) or Type A (Embassy Bilateral via Moroccan Ministry in Rabat).\n\u2022 Enter University Agency Number (Code de l'Agence Universitaire): \u3010 10001 \u3011 (Official Agency Code for NEFU).\n\nStep 2: University International Admissions Portal Registration:\n\u2022 Access the official university international admissions portal: https://www.nefu.edu.cn/\n\u2022 Complete the online application dossier and choose your desired major.\n\nStep 3: Document Legalization & Sworn Translation:\n\u2022 Prepare certified sworn translations (Traduction asserment\u00e9e) of your Moroccan degrees and transcripts into English or Chinese.\n\u2022 Legalize your Foreigner Physical Examination form and Moroccan Police Clearance (Casier Judiciaire).\n\nStep 4: Department Academic Review & Online Interview:\n\u2022 The academic faculty and professors will review your dossier and conduct an online academic interview via Voov / Tencent Meeting or Zoom.\n\nStep 5: Official Admission Notice & JW201/JW202 Visa Form:\n\u2022 Successful applicants receive the official Admission Notice and JW201/JW202 Visa Certificate by DHL to Morocco.\n\u2022 Apply for your X1 Long-Term Student Visa at the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Rabat (Souissi, Rabat).",
